serial number created when we signed alice certificate when we ran:
openssl x509 -req -in alice.csr -CA kind-ca.crt -CAkey kind-ca.key -CAcreateserial -out alice.crt -days 365
# Keep the serial file safe
mv kind-ca.srl ~/.kube/kind-ca.srl

# When signing future certificates, reference it
openssl x509 -req -in bob.csr -CA kind-ca.crt -CAkey kind-ca.key -CAserial ~/.kube/kind-ca.srl -out bob.crt -days 365

#it is important to keep track of serial keys so we dont have duplicates, in prod environment we use a private database to keep track of serial keys
